  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Dialogue and Feasibility of National Land Information System in Burundi</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The LAND-at-scale project in Burundi, Amohoro@Scale, organised a National Land Conference in December 2022. A broadly carried consensus of the Conference was that there should be a national land information and administration system (LAIS) that is bottom-up, flexible and relatively affordably. This was acknowledged by representatives of the national government of Burundi as well. However, the concept as agreed upon is still very abstract and unclear how to proceed towards the future. In the past, plans to aggregate information collected at decentralize levels, didn&#x2019;t receive much commitment from public authorities. Added to this is the institutional confusion and lack of collaboration between public authorities at local and central level to ensure the proper architecture of a LAIS. This poses a challenge for any land governance-related intervention that aims to provide durable solutions in a sector that is still very much at the beginning stages of the development of a national LAIS.The objective of the assignment is to build on the unprecedented momentum created by the National Land Conference to facilitate dialogues with government and other stakeholders and conduct a feasibility and capacity assessment on what is needed to move towards the development of a LAIS.</narrative>
  </description>
